What is the Feedbacker AI? Essentially, it’s an AI agent that acts as a player. It interacts with a game in development and provides feedback to the team by highlighting both the positives and the negatives. 
Think of it as a cost-effective, dynamic form of a beta tester. In theory, this sounds cool, right? Well, in practice, it’s a bit more complex. 

Here’s how I envisioned the solution:
First, we start by looking at the big picture, by selecting  the game genre, then we gather multiple successful games of that genre. 
We analyze reviews for each of those games and extract their sentiment. 
Next, we fetch specific keywords that are relevant in the gaming context. 
Using these keywords, that represent, in a way, game features, we check if they appear in our game. 
Finally, we generate a report showing how closely our game aligns with what the audience is looking for in future releases. 
